# AI Slop Cleanup

## Purpose

Detect and remove AI-generated noise patterns that degrade code quality without changing behavior.

## High-Confidence Removals

### Comments
- Narrate obvious code actions or restate the line below
- `// Loop through users`, `// Return the result`, `// Increment counter`
- Explain what the code does rather than why

### Defensive Code
- Broad `try/catch` blocks that don't match trusted call-path conventions
- Redundant null/undefined guards after validated parsing layers
- Over-defensive checks in internal functions with validated inputs

### Type Escapes (TypeScript)
- `as any` added only to suppress type errors
- Unsafe casts that bypass proper narrowing
- Ad-hoc type escape hatches instead of project utility types

### Abstraction Bloat
- Duplicate helper wrappers that only re-export existing behavior
- Generic helper functions used exactly once when inline is the norm
- Over-abstracted naming (`processDataHandlerManager`) when file style is simpler

### Logging
- Logging that repeats values already returned or thrown
- Debug logs left in production code paths

## Do NOT Remove

- Security boundaries, permission checks, input validation
- Error handling required by subsystem contracts
- Retries/timeouts/circuit breakers for reliability
- Observability hooks used by operations teams
- Business rule guards with non-obvious intent

## Scope Discipline

- Edit only changed hunks unless nearby fix required for coherence
- No non-requested refactors or unrelated formatting churn
- If uncertain whether a pattern is intentional, ask before changing behavior
- Preserve existing project idioms (error handling, logging, naming style)
